From 7f596892183ec8ec37bf29c8bc9097a253b1eae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 15:40:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(rfork): clear process-global layer registries before
 fallback re-init
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When RFork transfer fails (e.g. the previous fix's pre-transfer NaN, or any
future failure), RFork falls back to the default loader by re-running get_model
in the same worker process. initialize_model re-runs every layer __init__, which
re-registers each prefix into compilation_config.static_forward_context — a
process-global dict (not on the module instance) that survives 'del model'.
DeepseekV32IndexerCache.__init__ (and Attention/FusedMoE/Compressor/KDA/GDN)
raise 'Duplicate layer name: <prefix>' on the second registration, so the
fallback itself crashes and takes the worker down ('WorkerProc failed to start').

This affects DeepseekV2-family models including GLM-5 (GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM is
a DeepseekV2ForCausalLM subclass and reuses its Indexer/MLA stack).

Add _reset_process_global_model_state, mirroring
vllm.v1.worker.gpu.shutdown.free_before_shutdown, and call it in the fallback
except block after discarding the failed model and before the second
get_model. It clears static_forward_context, static_all_moe_layers, and
vllm.model_executor.layers.rotary_embedding._ROPE_DICT, each guarded so a
missing attribute on some vLLM version degrades gracefully.

Defense-in-depth: with the previous fix preventing the common trigger, this
ensures any future RFork failure no longer kills the worker.

- vLLM version: v0.22.1
- vLLM main: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/967c5c3bc38891f4465d3f4e99917ed837bb3833

Signed-off-by: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
---
